# Deal Atlas

- Player-facing prose and design docs are Korean. Code identifiers, file names, and formulas are English.
- The game is single-player and offline. Do not add accounts, analytics endpoints, or required network calls to the runtime.
- Money is an integer count of thousand USD (migrating from million KRW in M0). One currency, no FX. Locales change number formatting only. Do not accumulate currency in floating point. Multiples cross the Rust boundary as thousandths (7200 = 7.200x).
- Simulation math lives in `crates/sim-core`. Do not reimplement it in TypeScript. `src/sim` is the wasm loader and the view types and stays free of DOM, React, and MapLibre.
- The client fetches `public/content/universe.json` once to open a game and hands it to sim-core. Do not import generated content into the UI bundle. The screen draws only what `World::view` returns.
- Player-facing UI strings live in `src/i18n/locales/ko.json` (shared vocabulary) and one fragment per screen in `src/i18n/locales/ko/`. A key is defined once. Do not add en, ja, zh-Hans, or zh-Hant catalogs until copy is frozen. Storybook stories live in `stories/` and use those keys. `*.stories.tsx` is exempt from the UI string scan.
- Prices exist only when a deal event clears. A model multiple is not a share price. Do not add tickers or price paths.
- Company and person names in content are fictional. Do not paste real filings, articles, or addresses into the repo.
- Third-party art and audio are linked and credited, not vendored, unless the owner adds a small original file under `assets/`.
- The repository license is unset. Do not add an MIT/Apache/GPL grant, and do not relicense third-party code.
- Prefer a failing test that states an accounting identity over a silent plug.
- Screen CSS never uses `white-space: nowrap`. Layouts wrap.
- The view holds back what the player has not earned (ranges before an NDA, issues diligence has not found). Do not route around it by reading the save.
